Insights: α∈F is shifty ⇔ its polynomial A(x)=∑α(i)x^i (deg≤8) divides x^d+1 for some d>0 (after monomial shift). Hence A(x)=±x^c·∏Φ_m where each Φ_m is an even‑index cyclotomic (Φ_m|x^d+1) and all chosen m share the same 2‑adic exponent v₂(m).  

Data: even m≤30 with φ(m)≤8:  
t=1:{2(1),6(2),10(4),14(6),18(6),30(8)}  
t=2:{4(2),12(4),20(8)}  
t=3:{8(4),24(8)}  
t=4:{16(8)} (pair (m,deg)).  

Count: for each non‑empty subset S of a single t‑group with total degree D≤8, there are (9−D) shifts and 2 signs. Add empty set (±1) → 2·9=18.  

Total = 18 + Σ_{t} Σ_{S⊆group_t, S≠∅, Σdeg≤8} 2·(9−Σdeg) = **160**.  

Pitfalls: must enforce same v₂(m) for all factors; ignore odd‑index cyclotomics; include monomial factor x^c and overall sign.
